<.shell title="Checkboxes" current={:checkboxes}>
  <h1>Checkboxes</h1>
  <p class="lead">One setting, or several answers to one question.</p>
  <.used_on pages={[
    "taking attendance",
    "importing attendance",
    "reviewing group changes",
    "ID cards",
    "an organization"
  ]} />

  <div class="demo">
    <.input
      id="e-refresh"
      name="e-refresh"
      type="checkbox"
      label="Refresh from D4H every night"
      checked
    >
      SAR Duty refreshes at 02:00.
    </.input>
    <fieldset class="mb-p">
      <legend class="font-semibold">Activities to include</legend>
      <.hint>Meetings and public events count as events.</.hint>
      <label class="flex items-center gap-2 my-1"><input type="checkbox" checked /> Incidents</label>
      <label class="flex items-center gap-2 my-1"><input type="checkbox" checked /> Exercises</label>
      <label class="flex items-center gap-2 my-1"><input type="checkbox" /> Events</label>
    </fieldset>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A yes or no setting in a form with a save button.</li>
    <li>Picking any number of things from a list, such as rows to change.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Exactly one answer. Use <a href={page_path(:radios)}>radios</a>.</li>
    <li>
      A setting that takes effect when it's tapped. Use a <a href={page_path(:switch)}>switch</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>24px boxes, with the label beside them.</li>
    <li>Several that answer one question sit in a fieldset whose legend is the question.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    One setting is an <code>&lt;.input type="checkbox"&gt;</code>. A list is a
    <code>&lt;fieldset&gt;</code>
    of labelled checkboxes, as on the organization page.
  </p>
</.shell>
